%%{init: {'theme': 'neutral'}}%%
%% Payment lifecycle through the facilitator. Every terminal state carries a
%% non-null machine-readable reason (RFP 3.6; DECISIONS D-007, D-014, D-025).
%% Indexing outcomes never change the settlement outcome (DECISIONS D-015).
stateDiagram-v2
  [*] --> Received

  Received --> Rejected: envelope or kind uninterpretable — walras_* code
  Received --> Verifying: envelope valid, kind served

  Verifying --> Rejected: any verification MUST fails — scheme code (F-035)
  Verifying --> Verified: isValid true

  Verified --> Settling: POST /settle — full independent re-verification inside settle() (F-036)
  Settling --> SettleFailed: rejection, submission failure, or on-chain failure — scheme code
  Settling --> Settled: transaction SUCCESS, 64-hex hash in receipt (F-038)

  state "Settled — outcome fixed; indexing runs after and off this path (D-015)" as Settled
  Settled --> NotListed: no bazaar extension echoed by the client (F-032)
  Settled --> Indexing: bazaar extension present

  Indexing --> Indexed: EXTENSION-RESPONSES status success
  Indexing --> SoftDropped: client-attributable defect — status rejected + bazaar_* code (D-014)
  Indexing --> IndexerFault: walras-internal fault — header omitted, logged (D-025)

  Rejected --> [*]
  SettleFailed --> [*]
  NotListed --> [*]
  Indexed --> [*]
  SoftDropped --> [*]
  IndexerFault --> [*]

  note right of Rejected
    machine code + non-null human reason,
    on every rejection path (RFP 3.6)
  end note
  note right of SoftDropped
    settlement stays successful —
    only the catalog write is refused
    (proven live: EVIDENCE S3-4, S5-3)
  end note
